itoring of metabolite-induced electrical activity and voltage-dependent Ca2&#x0002b; currents in pancreatic islet B cells.</article-title><source>FEBS Lett</source><volume>251</volume><fpage>167</fpage><lpage>172</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2473925</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000983-Smith1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ashcroft</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name><name><surname>Rorsman</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>1990</year><article-title>Simultaneous recordings of glucose dependent electrical activity and ATP-regulated K(&#x0002b;)-currents in isolated mouse pancreatic beta-cells.</article-title><source>FEBS Lett</source><volume>261</volume><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>190</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2407553</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000983-Andreu1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Andreu</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Soria</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanchez-Andres</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Oscillation of gap junction electrical coupling in the mouse pancreatic islets of Langerhans.</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><volume>498</volume><issue>(Pt 3)</issue><fpage>753</fpage><lpage>761</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9051586</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000983-SanchezAndres1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sanchez-Andres</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name><name><surname>Gomis</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Valdeolmillos</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1995</year><article-title>The electrical activity of mouse pancreatic beta-cells recorded in vivo shows glucose-dependent oscillations.</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><volume>486</volume><issue>(Pt 1)</issue><fpage>223</fpage><lpage>228</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7562637</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000983-Valdeolmillos1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Valdeolmillos</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gomis</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanchez-Andres</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>In vivo synchronous membrane potential oscillations in mouse pancreatic beta-cells: lack of co-ordination between islets.</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><volume>493</volume><issue>(Pt 1)</issue><fpage>9</fpage><lpage>18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8735691</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000983-Nadal1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nadal</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Quesada</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Soria</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Homologous and heterologous asynchronicity between identified alpha-, beta- and delta-cells within intact islets of Langerhans in the mouse.</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><volume>517</volume><issue>(Pt 1)</issue><fpage>85</fpage><lpage>93</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10226151</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000983-Jonkers1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jonkers</surname><given-names>FC</given-names></name><name><surname>Jonas</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilon</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Henquin</su